    "text": "<p>A bimetallic strip consists of metals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. It is mounted rigidly as shown. The metal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> has higher coefficient of expansion compared to that of metal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. When the bimetallic strip is placed in a cold both, it will :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0059_2b4ade878328.png\" style=\"width: 166px; height: 127px;\" /></p>"
  },
